    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite passes (BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a `capacityWarning` flag that is set `true` when an owner's city already holds 40\u201349 owners at creation time (approaching the hard limit of 50), following the exact pattern the codebase already uses for `bulkSignupWarning`. The hard 409 rejection at 50 (`RejectFullOwnerCity`) is untouched.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`AssignOwnerCapacityWarning`** (new function class) \u2014 the single-responsibility step that computes the flag. It reuses `OwnerCities.size(...)` (the shared, case-insensitive city-count used by the rejection rule) so both rules count a city identically, and derives its upper bound from `RejectFullOwnerCity.CITY_CAPACITY` rather than duplicating the magic `50`. It runs after `BuildOwner` and before save, mutating the built `Owner` in place \u2014 mirroring `AssignOwnerBulkSignupWarning`.\n\n2. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired `assignCapacityWarning` into the pipeline between `assignBulkSignupWarning` and `assignPossibleDuplicate`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n\n3. **`Owner` model** \u2014 added the `capacityWarning` field (`@Column(name = \"capacity_warning\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"capacityWarning\", ignore = true)` on the `OwnerFieldsDto \u2192 Owner` request mapping (the field is response-only, so it has no request source); the `Owner \u2192 OwnerDto` direction maps automatically by name, exactly like `bulkSignupWarning`.\n\n5. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `capacityWarning` boolean to the owner response schema (generates the DTO field).\n\n6. **DB schemas** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `capacity_warning BOOLEAN` column.\n\n7. Updated `OwnerCities`' doc to name the new caller.\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreWarnsWhenApproachingCapacity` passes, and the full suite is green.",
